;; Reviewed 2026-10-28 by the user (written by Claude, for
;; doc/developer/language-extensions.md, "External variables", proposals
;; E1-E8). Why this is right:
;; - Each external variable is named by its linkage name in capitals in
;;   general mode, G^EXT_COUNTER, G^EXT_TABLE, G^EXT_PAIR, G^EXTSHR_LIMIT,
;;   G^EXT_FLAGS (["VMS"] ext_flags, its identifier its own name), declared
;;   .EXTERNAL in the order of first use, as an external procedure is
;;   (vax-external, section 7). None of them has storage in "the module's
;;   variables", which holds only i, sum and status.
;; - Imported ones, VaxExternalData's counter, table and pair, are reached
;;   by the same linkage names, not by VaxExternalData's mangled ones, and
;;   EXT_PAIR declared again here is the same symbol, so ADR(pair) and
;;   ADR(VaxExternalData.pair) are both MOVAB G^EXT_PAIR.
;; - A field is an offset from the symbol, G^EXT_PAIR+4, and an element is
;;   indexed, MOVAL G^EXT_TABLE[R0]; INCL on a set is BISL2 into it; a VAR
;;   actual is its address, MOVAB G^EXT_COUNTER and MOVAB G^EXTSHR_LIMIT.
;; - The initializer zeroes nothing: the values HAND-EXTDATA.MAR and
;;   HAND-EXTSHR.MAR gave are what the program starts with.
